# AEGIS

# Document 17 — AI Development Workflow + Tool Orchestration Architecture

**System:** AEGIS  
**Document:** 17 — AI Development Workflow + Tool Orchestration Architecture  
**Version:** 1.0  
**Status:** Master AI Engineering Workflow  
**Purpose:** Define exactly how humans, AI systems, development tools, design tools, documentation, testing, and source control collaborate to build AEGIS without architectural drift, hallucination, duplication, or uncontrolled implementation.

---

# 01. Purpose

AEGIS is being developed with multiple AI tools.

This creates enormous leverage.

It also creates a major engineering risk.

If ChatGPT, Claude, v0, OpenCode, and other tools are allowed to independently interpret the project, AEGIS can quickly become:

```text
different architectures
different terminology
different state models
different components
different assumptions
different implementations
```

This document prevents that.

The fundamental rule is:

> **AEGIS has one architecture and multiple AI workers.**

The AI tools do not collectively define AEGIS.

The approved AEGIS architecture defines AEGIS.

---

# 02. Core Principle

The human project owner controls the system.

The architecture documents control the technical truth.

AI tools accelerate specific parts of the workflow.

Therefore:

```text
HUMAN
  ↓
ARCHITECTURE
  ↓
AI SPECIALISTS
  ↓
IMPLEMENTATION
  ↓
VALIDATION
  ↓
HUMAN APPROVAL
```

Not:

```text
CHATGPT
CLAUDE
v0
OPENCODE
    ↓
different interpretations
    ↓
conflicting application
```

---

# 03. AEGIS AI Operating Model

AEGIS uses a **specialized AI orchestration model**.

Each tool receives a bounded responsibility.

| Tool | Primary Role | Authority |
|---|---|---|
| ChatGPT | Research, synthesis, specification, critique | Advisory |
| Claude | Architecture reasoning, decomposition, review | Advisory |
| v0 | High-fidelity UI exploration | Visual |
| OpenCode | Repository implementation | Execution |
| Git | Source control and history | Authoritative code history |
| Automated Tests | Behavioral verification | Validation |
| Human Owner | Final product and architecture authority | Final authority |

No AI tool has unilateral authority over the project.

